@nsobid-5CC7A76ED820CF4C45AA7B935C79307F

# THEATRHYTHM FINAL BAR LINE 1.0.5 - Double Buffering

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Forces a two-texture swapchain.
//
// Unity's NVN player creates the main window with 3 textures and picks how
// many are active from the device's max queued frames (clamped to 2..3),
// re-applying it with nvnWindowSetNumActiveTextures each frame. The device
// starts that value at 3 and the game never changes it: only the getter of
// QualitySettings.maxQueuedFrames is bound in this build. Starting it at 2,
// and building the window with 2 active textures, keeps the CPU at most one
// frame ahead of scanout.

@enabled
// GfxDevice max queued frames default
01315D4C 48008052   // MOV W8,#2 (was MOV W8,#3)
// nvnWindowBuilderSetNumActiveTextures at window creation
013307B8 41008052   // MOV W1,#2 (was LDR W1, texture count 3)
@stop

// Reverse-engineered against the Unity NX player in main (build id above).
// Every offset here was located by signature and byte-verified.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
